# Cloudflare Pages redirects
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# Format: [source] [destination] [code]   (one rule per line, # starts a comment)
# Limits: 2,000 static + 100 dynamic rules.
#
# IMPORTANT — domain-level rules are NOT supported here. A rule whose source
# includes a hostname (e.g. "https://www.coordcalc.com/* ...") is silently ignored
# by Pages. The www -> apex redirect therefore has to live in the Cloudflare zone:
#   Dashboard -> coordcalc.com -> Rules -> Redirect Rules -> Create rule
#     When incoming requests match: Hostname equals www.coordcalc.com
#     Then: Dynamic redirect to https://coordcalc.com/${http.request.uri.path} (301)
# See the "Custom domain" section of README.md.
#
# Nothing needs to be listed for the site's own pages: Pages already serves
# /dms-converter from dms-converter.html and redirects the *.html form for you.
# Add site-specific rules below as they come up, for example:
#
# /old-tool-name dms-converter 301
